{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1459761-magath-rites","id":1459761,"title":"Magath Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-12T12:50:44-07:00","id":1459761,"title":"Magath Rites","content":"So I am running a crossover game and one of the players is a Werewolf that has made a pack out of the player group. Recently the pack encountered two magaths that they picked up cuz Ghost-Wolf. One of them is a Bicycle/Madness spirit and the other is a House Fly/Human lust spirit. So yeah the various ilthums of the local hisil are going to be really mad at this pack cuz aiding and sheltering magath. Now, the player wants their character to learn rites from the two spirits in question....so I wanted suggestions for rites that could come from these two magaths or magaths in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-12T14:25:25-07:00","id":1459767,"title":"","content":"Since Magath are fusions of incompatible concepts, enacting their Rites may cause some unintended consequences. You may choose to make some of these Rites have trade-offs for the Packmates, or cause some sort of contamination within the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Pack consecrates a bicycle by reading genuine transcripts of mad conversations and spinning the wheels like in a Tibetan prayer. The next person to move the bicycle is stricken with the same mental condition as the author of the text. This may act as a lure for thieves, or as a barrier against the Pack's enemies.<br /> <br /> The Pack anoints a mentally ill person with bike grease and adorns them with reflective accessories. When treated as a travel guide, that person may lead the Pack to a site tied to that mental strain, either symbolically, or through personal experience. All participants must ride there on bicycles, and this can be done even if the destination is unknown, or otherwise blocked off.<br /> <br /> The Pack can mark a place, so that acts of lust within it will attract flies. It requires making a picture of a fly drawn with lipstick. Food will be filled with maggots, buzzing will fill the air and crawling and flying of insects will distract from carnal activities. This Rite is mostly used as punishment, sabotage or a very lazy way of chaperoning.<br /> <br /> The Pack marks a person to make them center of attention to flies and human beings. This aids in social endeavours, to the point that people are unbothered by the swarming insects. That indifference does not extend to the subject of the Rite, who has to grit their teeth all the way through. Also, after the Rite lapses, witnesses will realize something was amiss. Some have concluded that that the fly-covered figure they were wooed by was Beelzebub himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 09-12-2021, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T09:15:39-07:00","id":1459854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1459761-magath-rites?p=1459767#post1459767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Magath are fusions of incompatible concepts, enacting their Rites may cause some unintended consequences. You may choose to make some of these Rites have trade-offs for the Packmates, or cause some sort of contamination within the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The Pack consecrates a bicycle by reading genuine transcripts of mad conversations and spinning the wheels like in a Tibetan prayer. The next person to move the bicycle is stricken with the same mental condition as the author of the text. This may act as a lure for thieves, or as a barrier against the Pack's enemies.<br /> <br /> The Pack anoints a mentally ill person with bike grease and adorns them with reflective accessories. When treated as a travel guide, that person may lead the Pack to a site tied to that mental strain, either symbolically, or through personal experience. All participants must ride there on bicycles, and this can be done even if the destination is unknown, or otherwise blocked off.<br /> <br /> The Pack can mark a place, so that acts of lust within it will attract flies. It requires making a picture of a fly drawn with lipstick. Food will be filled with maggots, buzzing will fill the air and crawling and flying of insects will distract from carnal activities. This Rite is mostly used as punishment, sabotage or a very lazy way of chaperoning.<br /> <br /> The Pack marks a person to make them center of attention to flies and human beings. This aids in social endeavours, to the point that people are unbothered by the swarming insects. That indifference does not extend to the subject of the Rite, who has to grit their teeth all the way through. Also, after the Rite lapses, witnesses will realize something was amiss. Some have concluded that that the fly-covered figure they were wooed by was Beelzebub himself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are excellent suggestions,thank you!...The werewolf in question seems very focused on commiting spirit political suicide by making the pack like an open safe space for magath spirits....so the local courts won't be pleased with that. I now also have to consider the effect on these two spirits eating all of them Inspiration resonance from the pack locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-13T10:15:22-07:00","id":1459858,"title":"","content":"I'm happy that you liked them. Your game sounds exciting and I'm eager to know how it goes. Please, consider sharing some highlights from the session and your players' reaction to the Rites after you're done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T10:31:52-07:00","id":1461568,"title":"","content":"So update for those who are interested from the last couple of sessions.<br /> <br /> A strange monster has been operating near a college where several of the pcs have ties, specifically it laid strange eggs there and then after that a student was kidnapped. Now this monster had a dread power that basically made non-supernatural/supernaturally influenced people dismiss and ignore it's activities. So for example nobody thought it odd that this student vanished without a trace, except her roomie which is one of the human pack members. The Hunter of the Ascending Ones who is in the pack did quite a bit of digging around this, while the rest of the pack focused on studying the eggs they found.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet Vampire in the group on her end fed on a mortal with a strange condition which caused him to die and come back as a revenant despite having barely been fed on. He managed to find her while she was working night-shift at a local bar. She resolves to take him to the group. The Changeling of the Autumn court in the meantime has volunteered to have the Cum-Fly spirit fetter itself to him and is slowly exerting influence over his being. He views it as like a research opportunity and has also started to learn rites from it along with others in the pack.<br /> <br /> Anyway, last session the group had a meeting about the monster and the sudden revenant. The group decided the vampire had to uplift him so now the Pack has a baby vampire to take care of, while she is just a younging neonate herself. They also went to do more investigation and eventually managed to find the lair of the beast(not pun intended), the monster was away and had left the student there and its young. The student in question had lost both hands and feet, as well as all of her teeth because the creature/s feed on bone. The pack splits up taking the baby monsters and the student up to the surface while the Changeling and Werewolf hunt the monster down to slay it. The fight is quick but unfortunately, it scores a horrific attack combining Dread Attack with 5 successes leaving the Changeling blinded as a persistent condition and with the bleeding tilt as well.<br /> <br /> After the session the Cahalith and sole Uratha in the pack went into the Hisil to find a spirit of healing, she did not find one strong enough to restore the Changeling's sight. But she did learn of a Healing spirit unaffiliated with the local courts that might help. A spirit known as the Last Light, who has been hunted by the Uratha for years because of her more than notable tendency to cross over to the flesh to heal people n stuff. As Gathra to the local hospice spirit she got this information from she went out to &quot;remove&quot; a Magath spirit that used to be part of its brood. A spirit that was just the spirit of Hand-Sanitizer but ended up eating to much mud/earth essence and became a Magath. Combining Hand-Sanitizer with mud. She hunted the spirit down but rather than slay it she basically made it join the pack. So the pack is presently sheltering 3 Magaths.<br /> <br /> *sighs* now I am going to have to come up with rites from this spirit as well.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I hope this was a fun recap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T13:00:01-07:00","id":1461598,"title":"","content":"It sure was.<br /> <br /> If you need more Rites, have these two. Again, I assume performing them will wreck the local Resonance, somehow:<br /> <br /> The Pack meticulously cleans up an area, sterilizing all possible surfaces and objects, and then installing a sanitizer dispenser. That location then acts as if it possessed the Slick Environmental Tilt manifesting as invisible mud - thick and slippery. Only two types of people are immune to these effects. They must be similarly purified, up to their worn and carried belongings. Blood and tears do not disrupt that immunity, but sweat does. Alternatively, they must be thoroughly soiled - they, everything they have on them, and even their eyes covered in dirt or mud.<br /> <br /> The Pack acquires a manual for disinfection - even a poster from a toilet will do. They then read from it, following the instructions to the letter, while smearing their subject in mud. They then bury that person within a layer of dirt inside a place of healing - any place with the right Resonance will do. While giving them means to breathe is not technically necessary for the Rite, it's strongly recommended. Over the next few hours, the soil pulls out all pathogens from the patient, curing minor infections and helping against major ones.<br /> <br /> As a side-note. I can imagine their new Magath friend standing in the corner with Cum-Fly, both doing nervous rubbing motions with their forelimbs. They may not understand each other or even themselves anymore, but this one thing feels safe and familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":".  In the last paragraph I was referring to the grooming motions that flies do. Only later did I realize that in Cum-Fly's case my writing could be interpreted... differently. 09-27-2021, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:34:48-07:00","id":1461730,"title":"","content":"Oh the players have declared that they are going to keep pursuing adding more Magaths to the pack so I thought as a fun little thing people here could put forth magath concepts. I might not pick all of them but it is a chance for people to hear about weird spirits that should not be actually being used as npcs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Concept, some personality notes, and an optional backstory note would be ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T11:51:56-07:00","id":1461735,"title":"","content":"Ohhh we have the first usage of a Magath Rite...that vampire is now going to be covered in Cum-Fly resonance...strange little motes might come about due to feeding on it.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet vampire cursed a &quot;rival&quot; vampire who has harassed her with his ghouls and tried to have her beat up. Welp now every time lust comes up he is going to get flies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T07:18:22-07:00","id":1462651,"title":"","content":"Two more Magaths found and recruited:<br /> <br /> A spirit of Prophecy and Hairspray<br /> <br /> And a spirit of Immortality and Urban Decay(a spirit born from the obsession of an immortal who then ate a lesser blightling)<br /> <br /> The totem has also rapidly advanced from rank 1 to 3 and is now A spirit of Infectious Inspiration for the Downtrodden...aka she has been feasting on disease spirits and evolved her nature to be the idea of inspiration as something contagious while also assosciating with outcasts and being forced to allow Magath into it's pack.<br /> <br /> Session summary:<br /> <br /> So a Deviant has joined the game who is being hunted by evil Mensa... One of the ghouls following the vampire around was captured and the group then used a combination of Auspex, Changeling contracts, and elixirs to pull out all the information of the ghoul. The group then had the Deviant eat it's memories and they left the traumatized ghoul out to be found..Problem said ghoul is out on a loan from one of the Barons of the Invictus so the group has potentially made a really notable enemy there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T07:46:48-07:00","id":1462653,"title":"","content":"Rite design isn't my forte, but an observation on magath that may help generally: If you look at example magath throughout the books, a trend that emerges is that hybrids who make it work tend to have common ground to their component resonances that imply a theme.<br /> <br /> Magath are ostracized by most spirits because their portfolios don't emerge from natural associations, but even desperate feeding circumstances will still see a spirit try to eat something <i>kind of</i> related to what it is, metaphorically strained or not \u2014 and if that's not how it got there, knowing how it got there (particularly if some spiritually-traumatic event or other non-&quot;a wizard did it&quot; origin is involved) will provide symbolic grounding for What This Magath Is.<br /> <br /> Spirits may not be the same thing as ghosts, but they <i>are</i> creatures of history and the sum of their parts; gradual divergence from repeating the circumstances of their birth (and death and rebirth) is how they shuffle into the impurity of the higher Ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T03:12:04-07:00","id":1463211,"title":"","content":"I don't mind homebrew that breaks away from the normal rules, but where the rules are misunderstood I feel compelled to clarify. Frankly, this is a case where the rules are ambiguous. Where do Rites come from? Aside from the obvious, that is. Some entrees in the Rites section of the second edition make it sound as though Rites come from actions and broad patterns, others describe them as a &quot;pact.&quot; Maybe they have multiple origins? In any case I am not any more convinced that mere magaths give rise to new Rites than I am convinced that they give rise to new Gifts, though I can't say you're wrong in any version I remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T03:33:24-07:00","id":1463213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1459761-magath-rites?p=1463211#post1463211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind homebrew that breaks away from the normal rules, but where the rules are misunderstood I feel compelled to clarify. Frankly, this is a case where the rules are ambiguous. Where do Rites come from? Aside from the obvious, that is. Some entrees in the Rites section of the second edition make it sound as though Rites come from actions and broad patterns, others describe them as a &quot;pact.&quot; Maybe they have multiple origins? In any case I am not any more convinced that mere magaths give rise to new Rites than I am convinced that they give rise to new Gifts, though I can't say you're wrong in any version I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh they are not the creator of the rites or the ones empowering said rites. I should make it clear it is more that these spirits know particularly strange and alien aspects of the laws of the Shadow. There are many rites that the people does not know that claimed and spirits are quite willing to teach to other people, so I found it reasonable that Magaths would know quite weird secrets to pass along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T02:25:40-08:00","id":1531870,"title":"","content":"Necrothread time. In another Werewolf game i am running the pack are going to hunt(most likely) a Magath that is a spirit of Revelry and Cavern Rock(a spirit of parties got trapped in the earth and started eating rock spirits to survive but changed as a result). I am considering giving them a Shadow Occultist servant who the pack can find on their territory and I was wondering anyone could help me ponder up some spooky rites for this antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T03:15:39-08:00","id":1531873,"title":"","content":"Since it's a Rite for the antagonist, I will skip over how it's performed and go straight to the effects:<br /> <br /> The first Rite is simple - the Occultist prepares a party, but replacing some of the food with small rocks or grit. If successful, any unwarned participants of the party will believe the minerals to be normal food, even as their teeth break and their insides are shredded. Any medical emergencies or incongruities stemming from that source alone, like people slurring their speech or lying in pain on the floor will be ignored by the revelers until sunrise.<br /> <br /> The second Rite must take place within a prominent Stone Resonance, be it a cave or an obvious stone circle. As the Rite culminates, all unwary or willing participants are placed in a suspended animation of sorts - immobile, unaging and experiencing only an ecstatic stupor. This lasts indefinitely until somebody tries to physically &quot;wake&quot; one of the revelers. The unfortunate(?) rescue subject then turns to stone permanently (still ensouled and experiencing the joy of the party). All other party goers return to normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}